      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_41848237",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: shiba_inu_transphobic_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a Shiba Inu dog with the text 'I'm not transphobic i just don't like 'em'. The meme uses the dog's innocent, slightly smug expression to mock or dismiss transphobia by implying that disliking transgender people is not the same as being transphobic. This is a harmful and hateful trope that trivializes the serious nature of transphobia, which is a form of discrimination and prejudice against transgender individuals based on their gender identity. The meme attempts to normalize or excuse transphobic attitudes by framing them as a personal preference rather than a harmful bias, which is a direct attack on the protected characteristic of gender identity. The use of a dog as the subject is a common meme format that can be used to dehumanize or trivialize the subject matter, further contributing to the hateful intent.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c5ef0a46"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
